Purpose of Position &nbsp;

As a Senior Global Account Manager, you will manage the Spanish affiliate programmes of some of Awin’s key international clients, working closely with client stakeholders and Awin teams across multiple markets. &nbsp;

You will own the local strategy and performance of your accounts while ensuring alignment with the wider global client strategy. Acting as a trusted advisor, you will combine strong affiliate expertise, commercial thinking and market insight to identify growth opportunities and deliver long-term value for both clients and Awin. &nbsp;

As a senior member of the team, you will work with a high degree of autonomy, contribute to cross-market initiatives and share your expertise and best practices with colleagues. &nbsp;

Key Tasks

• Own and develop the Spanish affiliate strategy for an assigned portfolio of strategic global clients. &nbsp;

• Build strong relationships with senior client stakeholders, acting as a trusted advisor and extension of their team. &nbsp;

• Develop strategic account roadmaps aligned with client objectives, global priorities and Spanish market opportunities. &nbsp;

• Work closely with Awin Account Managers across markets to ensure alignment, consistency and a high level of service. &nbsp;

• Analyse programme performance and turn data, market trends and competitor insights into clear recommendations and actions. &nbsp;

• Identify opportunities for organic growth, upselling, cross-selling and improved client retention. &nbsp;

• Develop the publisher strategy, strengthening existing partnerships and identifying new local and international opportunities. &nbsp;

• Provide strategic guidance around Awin technology, tracking, attribution and relevant product solutions. &nbsp;

• Proactively manage challenges and risks, taking ownership and escalating when appropriate. &nbsp;

• Lead client business reviews, strategic presentations and commercial conversations. &nbsp;

• Contribute to pitches, internal projects and cross-functional initiatives. &nbsp;

• Act as a senior reference within the team, sharing expertise, best practices and supporting the development of colleagues. &nbsp;

Skills &amp; Expertise &nbsp;

• 3+ years of experience in affiliate marketing, performance marketing, ecommerce or a related digital marketing environment. &nbsp;

• Strong understanding of affiliate marketing and its role within the wider digital marketing mix. &nbsp;

• Proven experience managing strategic or complex client accounts with a high degree of autonomy. &nbsp;

• Experience working with international stakeholders and cross-market teams. &nbsp;

• Strong analytical skills, with the ability to translate data into insights, recommendations and commercial opportunities. &nbsp;

• Strong client management, negotiation and influencing skills. &nbsp;

• Confidence presenting strategic and commercial recommendations to senior stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Commercial mindset with the ability to identify growth, upselling and cross-selling opportunities. &nbsp;

• Strong ownership, decision-making and problem-solving skills. &nbsp;

• Ability to manage multiple priorities and remain solutions-focused in a fast-paced environment. &nbsp;

• Collaborative mindset and ability to share knowledge, mentor colleagues and contribute to team development. &nbsp;

• Good knowledge of Salesforce, Excel and PowerPoint. Experience with Power BI, Tableau or Asana is a plus. &nbsp;

• Full professional proficiency in English is essential, as the role involves regular meetings, presentations and strategic coordination with international clients and Awin teams. &nbsp;

• Professional proficiency in Spanish. &nbsp;

